/*!
@defgroup wku
@ingroup mod_system Wakeup Unit (WKU)
@brief Wakeup-source management module for power-down recovery in the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The Wakeup Unit (WKU) monitors external wakeup pins, the reset pin, and a set
of internal low-power module requests so the system can exit power-down mode.
The driver layer provides instance-based configuration APIs, while the hardware
access layer exposes register-level helpers used internally by the driver.

@section wku_features Key Features
- Supports device-dependent external wakeup channel counts through
  `FEATURE_WKU_MAX_CHANNEL_COUNT`.
- Supports rising-edge, falling-edge, both-edge, or disabled detection per
  external wakeup channel.
- Supports optional digital filtering for external wakeup pins.
- Supports reset-pin wakeup configuration with optional digital filtering.
- Supports enabling wakeup requests from internal low-power modules such as
  RTC, lpTMR0, and ACMP.
- Supports optional pin isolation on devices that define
  `FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_PIN_ISOLATION`.

@section wku_standards Supported Modes

The following table summarizes the wakeup paths handled by the WKU driver:

| Wakeup Path           | Primary APIs                                      | Key Parameters                                       | Notes |
|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|-------|
| External pin wakeup   | WKU_DRV_InitPinWakeup(), WKU_DRV_SetPinWakeupConfig() | `hwChannel`, `edgeEvent`, `filterEn`, `filterClkSrc` | Channel count is device-dependent. |
| Reset-pin wakeup      | WKU_DRV_InitReset(), WKU_DRV_GetResetDefaultConfig() | `wakeupEn`, `filterEn`, `filterClkSrc`               | Filter clock selection is optional by feature macro. |
| Internal module wakeup| WKU_DRV_EnableModuleWakeup(), WKU_DRV_DisableModuleWakeup() | `moduleID` from `wku_wakeup_module_t`                | Module availability depends on the device. |
| Pin isolation         | WKU_DRV_SetPinIsolation()                         | `enable`                                             | Available only when `FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_PIN_ISOLATION` is enabled. |

@subsection wku_filter_clock Shared Filter Clock Sources
When `FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_FILTER_CLOCK_SEL` is enabled, the WKU filtering logic
can select one of the following clock sources:

| Clock Source          | Description |
|-----------------------|-------------|
| WKU_FILTER_CLK_SIRC   | Use the SIRC clock as filter input. |
| WKU_FILTER_CLK_SXOSC  | Use the SXOSC clock as filter input. |

@section wku_arch Module Architecture

The WKU module is organized as a two-layer driver:

@verbatim
+----------------------------------------------+
|              Application Code                |
|         (calls WKU_DRV_* functions)          |
+----------------------------------------------+
|          WKU Driver Layer (wku_driver.h/c)   |
|  - Instance-based configuration APIs         |
|  - Pin wakeup, reset wakeup, and module      |
|    wakeup orchestration                      |
+----------------------------------------------+
|     WKU HW Access Layer (wku_hw_access.h)    |
|  - Inline register access helpers            |
|  - Pin flags, PCR/RPCR/MER bit control       |
+----------------------------------------------+
|           WKU Peripheral Hardware            |
|      (PCR[], PFR[], RPCR, MER registers)     |
+----------------------------------------------+
@endverbatim

@subsection wku_arch_driver Driver Layer (wku_driver.h)
Application code should use the `WKU_DRV_*` APIs declared in wku_driver.h.
These functions accept a zero-based WKU instance index and resolve the
peripheral base address internally through `WKU_BASE_PTRS`.

@subsection wku_arch_hw Hardware Access Layer (wku_hw_access.h)
This internal layer provides register-level inline helpers that are grouped into
four capability areas:
- **Pin Flag Management** - WKU_ClearPinWakeupFlag()
- **Pin Wakeup Control** - WKU_SetWakeueEdgeEvent(), WKU_EnableFilter(), WKU_EnablePinInterrupt()
- **Reset Wakeup Control** - WKU_EnableResetPin(), WKU_EnableResetPinFilter(), WKU_SetResetPinFilterClock()
- **Module Wakeup Control** - WKU_EnableModuleWakeup()

@section wku_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection wku_config_pin wku_pin_wakeup_cfg_t Fields
| Field        | Type                      | Description | Default from WKU_DRV_GetPinWakeupDefaultConfig() |
|--------------|---------------------------|-------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| hwChannel    | uint8_t                   | WKU hardware channel index programmed in `PCR[]`. | Channel index of the array entry. |
| wakeupEn     | bool                      | Requested wakeup-enable state tracked by the configuration. | Not initialized by the helper; set explicitly in application code. |
| edgeEvent    | wku_edge_event_t          | Edge-detection mode for the selected channel. | WKU_EDGE_BOTH |
| filterEn     | bool                      | Enables or bypasses the channel digital filter. | false |
| filterClkSrc | wku_filter_clock_source_t | Shared filter clock source when supported. | WKU_FILTER_CLK_SIRC |

@subsection wku_config_reset wku_reset_cfg_t Fields
| Field        | Type                      | Description | Default from WKU_DRV_GetResetDefaultConfig() |
|--------------|---------------------------|-------------|----------------------------------------------|
| wakeupEn     | bool                      | Enables reset-pin wakeup requests. | true |
| filterEn     | bool                      | Enables reset-pin digital filtering. | true |
| filterClkSrc | wku_filter_clock_source_t | Shared filter clock source when supported. | WKU_FILTER_CLK_SIRC |

@subsection wku_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro                                 | Description |
|---------------------------------------|-------------|
| FEATURE_WKU_MAX_CHANNEL_COUNT         | Number of external wakeup channels supported by the device. |
| FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_FILTER_CLOCK_SEL  | Set to 1 when WKU exposes the filter clock selection field. |
| FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_PIN_ISOLATION     | Set to 1 when the device supports pad-state isolation in power-down mode. |
| WKU_INSTANCE_COUNT                    | Number of WKU peripheral instances available on the device. |

@section wku_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection wku_usage_pins Pattern 1: Configure External Pin Wakeup Channels
Use this pattern when one or more GPIO-backed wakeup channels must bring the
device out of power-down mode:

@code{.c}
#define INST_WKU              (0U)
#define WKU_USED_CHANNELS     (2U)

wku_pin_wakeup_cfg_t pinConfig[WKU_USED_CHANNELS] = { 0 };

int main(void)
{
    pinConfig[0U].hwChannel = 3U;
    pinConfig[0U].wakeupEn = true;
    pinConfig[0U].edgeEvent = WKU_EDGE_RISING;
    pinConfig[0U].filterEn = true;
#if FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_FILTER_CLOCK_SEL
    pinConfig[0U].filterClkSrc = WKU_FILTER_CLK_SIRC;
#endif

    pinConfig[1U].hwChannel = 7U;
    pinConfig[1U].wakeupEn = true;
    pinConfig[1U].edgeEvent = WKU_EDGE_FALLING;
    pinConfig[1U].filterEn = false;
#if FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_FILTER_CLOCK_SEL
    pinConfig[1U].filterClkSrc = WKU_FILTER_CLK_SIRC;
#endif

    WKU_DRV_InitPinWakeup(INST_WKU, WKU_USED_CHANNELS, pinConfig);

    for (;;)
    {
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection wku_usage_reset Pattern 2: Enable Reset-Pin and Internal Module Wakeup
Use this pattern when reset-pin wakeup and an internal low-power source are
part of the low-power recovery flow:

@code{.c}
#define INST_WKU (0U)

wku_reset_cfg_t resetConfig;

int main(void)
{
    WKU_DRV_GetResetDefaultConfig(&resetConfig);
    resetConfig.wakeupEn = true;
    resetConfig.filterEn = true;
#if FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_FILTER_CLOCK_SEL
    resetConfig.filterClkSrc = WKU_FILTER_CLK_SIRC;
#endif

    WKU_DRV_InitReset(INST_WKU, &resetConfig);
    WKU_DRV_EnableModuleWakeup(INST_WKU, (uint8_t)WKU_lpTMR0_WAKEUP);

#if FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_PIN_ISOLATION
    WKU_DRV_SetPinIsolation(true);
#endif

    for (;;)
    {
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection wku_usage_service Pattern 3: Service Wakeup Flags and Clear Configuration
Use this pattern after wakeup to acknowledge the source and release the WKU
resources that are no longer needed:

@code{.c}
#define INST_WKU          (0U)
#define WKU_SERVICE_CH    (3U)

void WKU_AfterWakeup(void)
{
    WKU_DRV_ClearPinWakeupFlag(INST_WKU, WKU_SERVICE_CH);
    WKU_DRV_ClearPinWakeupConfig(INST_WKU, WKU_SERVICE_CH);
    WKU_DRV_DisableModuleWakeup(INST_WKU, (uint8_t)WKU_lpTMR0_WAKEUP);
    WKU_DRV_DeinitReset(INST_WKU);

#if FEATURE_WKU_SUPPORT_PIN_ISOLATION
    WKU_DRV_SetPinIsolation(false);
#endif
}
@endcode

@section wku_api API Quick Reference

@subsection wku_api_pin_init Pin Wakeup Initialization & De-initialization
| Function                             | Description |
|--------------------------------------|-------------|
| WKU_DRV_InitPinWakeup()              | Apply a table of external pin wakeup channel configurations. |
| WKU_DRV_DeinitPinWakeup()            | Clear all external pin wakeup channel settings. |
| WKU_DRV_GetPinWakeupDefaultConfig()  | Populate default channel settings for all supported wakeup pins. |

@subsection wku_api_pin_ctrl Pin Wakeup Channel Control
| Function                             | Description |
|--------------------------------------|-------------|
| WKU_DRV_SetPinWakeupConfig()         | Apply one external pin wakeup channel configuration. |
| WKU_DRV_ClearPinWakeupConfig()       | Clear one external pin wakeup channel configuration. |
| WKU_DRV_SetPinWakeupNormalMode()     | Put a channel into the driver's normal operating mode. |
| WKU_DRV_SetPinWakeupSleepMode()      | Put a channel into the driver's sleep-mode policy. |
| WKU_DRV_SetPinWakeupEdgeEvent()      | Program the edge-detection mode for one channel. |
| WKU_DRV_ClearPinWakeupFlag()         | Acknowledge the wakeup flag of one channel. |

@subsection wku_api_reset Reset Wakeup Control
| Function                             | Description |
|--------------------------------------|-------------|
| WKU_DRV_InitReset()                  | Configure reset-pin wakeup behavior. |
| WKU_DRV_DeinitReset()                | Clear reset-pin wakeup settings. |
| WKU_DRV_GetResetDefaultConfig()      | Populate the default reset-pin wakeup configuration. |

@subsection wku_api_module Internal Module Wakeup Control
| Function                             | Description |
|--------------------------------------|-------------|
| WKU_DRV_EnableModuleWakeup()         | Enable a selected internal module wakeup source. |
| WKU_DRV_DisableModuleWakeup()        | Disable a selected internal module wakeup source. |

@subsection wku_api_hw Internal HW Access Helpers
| Function                             | Description |
|--------------------------------------|-------------|
| WKU_ClearPinWakeupFlag()             | Clear the flag bit for one pin wakeup channel. |
| WKU_SetWakeueEdgeEvent()             | Program the edge-selection bits for one channel. |
| WKU_EnableFilter()                   | Enable or bypass channel filtering. |
| WKU_EnablePinInterrupt()             | Enable or disable the pin interrupt path. |
| WKU_EnableResetPin()                 | Enable or disable reset-pin wakeup requests. |
| WKU_EnableResetPinFilter()           | Enable or disable reset-pin digital filtering. |
| WKU_SetResetPinFilterClock()         | Select the shared WKU filter clock source. |
| WKU_EnableModuleWakeup()             | Set or clear an internal module wakeup enable bit. |

@section wku_notes Important Notes

@subsection wku_notes_power Low-Power Flow Dependency
Configure the WKU module as part of the system's low-power entry and exit flow.
Clocking and wakeup sequencing are coordinated with @ref clock_manager and
@ref power_manager.

@subsection wku_notes_defaults Default Configuration Caveat
@warning WKU_DRV_GetPinWakeupDefaultConfig() initializes `hwChannel`,
`edgeEvent`, `filterEn`, and `filterClkSrc` (when supported), but it does
not initialize `wakeupEn`. The application must set that field explicitly
before reusing the configuration entry.

@subsection wku_notes_channels Device Variations
The number of external pin wakeup channels is not fixed across devices.
Always size channel-related logic around `FEATURE_WKU_MAX_CHANNEL_COUNT`.

@subsection wku_notes_filter Shared Filter Clock
@note The filter clock source is configured through a shared WKU register field.
Changing the filter clock affects the filtering logic used by WKU wakeup paths
that rely on that shared setting.

@subsection wku_notes_isolation Pin Isolation
@warning If pin isolation is enabled before entering power-down mode, disable
it after the MCU reinitializes its pin configuration on wakeup. Leaving pad
isolation enabled can prevent the application from restoring normal pin behavior.

@section wku_integration Integration Guide

@subsection wku_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source file must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/wku/wku_driver.c
@endverbatim

The low-level helper layer is header-only and is pulled in through:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/wku/wku_hw_access.h
@endverbatim

@subsection wku_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directory to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection wku_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required for this module. Device feature
macros such as `FEATURE_WKU_*` are supplied by the selected device header.

@subsection wku_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager - Required for clock and wakeup sequencing setup.
- @ref power_manager - Required for low-power entry and recovery integration.

*/
